<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucknow</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucknow is the capital of the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the river Gomti. It became the capital of the Nawabs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a> in 1775 and flourished as a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urdu">Urdu</a> poetry, music, architecture and cuisine. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-rebellion-of-1857">Indian Rebellion of 1857</a> its British Residency was besieged for months, and the city remains known for its Nawabi monuments and courtly culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucknow.jpg" alt="Lucknow" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mohit · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harzratganj_Market,_Lucknow.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
